<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="AMO" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Amos</para>
  <para style="mt">Amos</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The words of ‘Amos <char style="add">[burden]</char>, who was among the herdsmen of T’koa <char style="add">[a stockade]</char>, which he saw concerning Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in the days of ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and in the days of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, two years before the earthquake.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he said, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will roar from Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>, and utter his voice from Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; and the habitations of the shepherds shall mourn, and the top of Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char> shall wither.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; For three transgressions of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, and for four, I will not turn away <char style="add">[the punishment]</char> thereof; because they have threshed Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> with threshing instruments of iron:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But I will send a fire into the house of Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char>, which shall devour the palaces of Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />I will break also the bar of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, and cut off the inhabitant from the plain of On <char style="add">[vanity]</char>, and him that holds the scepter from the house of ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char>: and the people of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> shall go into captivity unto Kir <char style="add">[wall]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; For three transgressions of ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char>, and for four, I will not turn away <char style="add">[the punishment]</char> thereof; because they carried away captive the whole captivity, to deliver <char style="add">[them]</char> up to Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But I will send a fire on the wall of ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char>, which shall devour the palaces thereof:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I will cut off the inhabitant from Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, and him that holds the scepter from Ashkelon <char style="add">[The Fire of Infamy: I shall be Weighed]</char>, and I will turn my hand against ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>: and the remnant of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> shall perish, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; For three transgressions of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, and for four, I will not turn away <char style="add">[the punishment]</char> thereof; because they delivered up the whole captivity to Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and remembered not the brotherly covenant:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But I will send a fire on the wall of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, which shall devour the palaces thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; For three transgressions of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and for four, I will not turn away <char style="add">[the punishment]</char> thereof; because he did pursue his brother with the sword, and did cast off all pity, and his anger did tear perpetually, and he kept his wrath forever:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But I will send a fire upon Teman <char style="add">[south]</char>, which shall devour the palaces of Botzrah <char style="add">[sheepfold or fortress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; For three transgressions of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and for four, I will not turn away <char style="add">[the punishment]</char> thereof; because they have ripped up the women with child of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, that they might enlarge their border:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But I will kindle a fire in the wall of Rabbah <char style="add">[Great]</char>, and it shall devour the palaces thereof, with shouting in the day of battle, with a tempest in the day of the whirlwind:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And their king shall go into captivity, he and his princes together, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; For three transgressions of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and for four, I will not turn away <char style="add">[the punishment]</char> thereof; because he burned the bones of the king of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> into lime:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />But I will send a fire upon Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and it shall devour the palaces of K’riot <char style="add">[Surrounded by a Wall]</char>: and Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> shall die with tumult, with shouting, <char style="add">[and]</char> with the sound of the trumpet:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I will cut off the judge from the midst thereof, and will slay all the princes thereof with him, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; For three transgressions of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and for four, I will not turn away <char style="add">[the punishment]</char> thereof; because they have despised the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and have not kept his commandments, and their lies caused them to err, after the which their fathers have walked:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />But I will send a fire upon Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and it shall devour the palaces of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; For three transgressions of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and for four, I will not turn away <char style="add">[the punishment]</char> thereof; because they sold the righteous for silver, and the poor for a pair of shoes;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />That pant after the dust of the earth on the head of the poor, and turn aside the way of the meek: and a man and his father will go in unto the <char style="add">[same]</char> maid, to Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char> my holy name:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they lay <char style="add">[themselves]</char> down upon clothes laid to pledge by every altar, and they drink the wine of the condemned <char style="add">[in]</char> the house of their god.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Yet destroyed I the Emori <char style="add">[Rebellious Highlanders]</char> before them, whose height <char style="add">[was]</char> like the height of the cedars, and he <char style="add">[was]</char> strong as the oaks; yet I destroyed his fruit from above, and his roots from beneath.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Also I brought you up from the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and led you forty years through the wilderness, to possess the land of the Emori <char style="add">[Rebellious Highlanders]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And I raised up of your sons for prophets, and of your young men for N’zirim <char style="add">[consecrated ones]</char>. <char style="add">[Is it]</char> not even thus, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">2f</char> gave the N’zirim <char style="add">[consecrated ones]</char> wine to drink; and commanded the prophets, saying, Prophesy not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Behold, I am pressed under you, as a cart is pressed <char style="add">[that is]</char> full of sheaves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Therefore the flight shall perish from the swift, and the strong shall not strengthen his force, neither shall the mighty deliver himself:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Neither shall he stand that handles the bow; and <char style="add">[he that is]</char> swift of foot shall not deliver <char style="add">[himself]</char>: neither shall he that rides the horse deliver himself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And <char style="add">[he that is]</char> courageous among the mighty shall flee away naked in that day, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Hear this word that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken against you, O people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, against the whole family which I brought up from the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />You only have I known of all the families of the earth: therefore I will punish you for all your iniquities.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Can two walk together, except they be agreed?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Will a lion roar in the forest, when he has no prey? will a young lion cry out of his den, if he have taken nothing?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Can a bird fall in a snare upon the earth, where no trap <char style="add">[is]</char> for him? shall <char style="add">[one]</char> take up a snare from the earth, and have taken nothing at all?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Shall a trumpet be blown in the city, and the people not be afraid? shall there be evil in a city, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has not done <char style="add">[it]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Surely the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> will do nothing, but he reveals his secret unto his servants the prophets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The lion has roared, who will not fear? the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> has spoken, who can but prophesy?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Publish in the palaces at Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, and in the palaces in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and say, Assemble yourselves upon the mountains of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and behold the great tumults in the midst thereof, and the oppressed in the midst thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />For they know not to do right, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, who store up violence and robbery in their palaces.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; An adversary <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> even round about the land; nd he shall bring down you<char style="ord">i</char> strength from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> palaces shall be spoiled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; As the shepherd takes out of the mouth of the lion two legs, or a piece of an ear; so shall the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> be taken out that dwell in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> in the corner of a bed, and in Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver] [in]</char> a couch.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Hear you<char style="ord">2f</char>, and testify in the house of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, the God-Elohe <char style="add">[The Living Word]</char> <char style="pn">(The Many Powered)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />That in the day that I shall visit the transgressions of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> upon him I will also visit the altars of Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>: and the horns of the altar shall be cut off, and fall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And I will strike the winter house with the summer house; and the houses of ivory shall perish, and the great houses shall have an end, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Hear this word, your<char style="ord">2f</char> cattle of Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char>, that <char style="add">[are]</char> in the mountain of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, which oppress the poor, which crush the needy, which say to their masters, Bring, and let us drink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />The Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> has sworn by his holiness, that, lo, the days shall come upon you, that he will take you away with hooks, and your posterity with fishhooks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall go out at the breaches, every <char style="add">[cow at that which is]</char> before her; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall cast <char style="add">[them]</char> into the palace, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Come to Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and transgress; at Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char> multiply transgression; and bring your sacrifices every morning, <char style="add">[and]</char> your tithes after three years:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And offer a sacrifice of thanksgiving with leaven, and proclaim <char style="add">[and]</char> publish the free offerings: for this likes you, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I also have given you famine in all your cities, and lack of bread in all your places: yet have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not returned unto me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And also I have withheld the rain from you, when <char style="add">[there were]</char> yet three months to the harvest: and I caused it to rain upon one city, and caused it not to rain upon another city: one piece was rained upon, and the piece whereupon it rained not withered.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />So two <char style="add">[or]</char> three cities wandered unto one city, to drink water; but they were not satisfied: yet have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not returned unto me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />I have smitten you with blasting and mildew: when your gardens and your vineyards and your fig trees and your olive trees increased, the palmerworm devoured <char style="add">[them]</char>: yet have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not returned unto me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />I have sent among you the pestilence after the manner of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: your young men have I slain with the sword, and have taken away your horses; and I have made the stink of your camps to come up unto your nostrils: yet have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not returned unto me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />I have overthrown <char style="add">[some]</char> of you, as God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> overthrew S’dom <char style="add">[Burning]</char> and ‘Amora <char style="add">[Submersion]</char>, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> were as a torch plucked out of the burning: yet have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not returned unto me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Therefore thus will I do unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: <char style="add">[and]</char> because I will do this unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, prepare to meet your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />For, lo, he that forms the mountains, and creates the wind, and declares unto man what <char style="add">[is]</char> his thought, that makes the morning darkness, and treads upon the high places of the earth, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, The God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, <char style="add">[is]</char> his name.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Hear you<char style="ord">2f</char> this word which I take up against you, <char style="add">[even]</char> a lamentation, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />The virgin of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> is fallen; she shall no more rise: she is forsaken upon her land; <char style="add">[there is]</char> none to raise her up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; The city that went out <char style="add">[by]</char> a thousand shall leave an hundred, and that which went forth <char style="add">[by]</char> an hundred shall leave ten, to the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />For thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Seek you<char style="ord">2f</char> me, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall live:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />But seek not Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, nor enter into Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, and pass not to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>: for Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char> shall surely go into captivity, and Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> shall come to nothing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall live; lest he break out like fire in the house of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>, and devour <char style="add">[it]</char>, and <char style="add">[there be]</char> none to quench <char style="add">[it]</char> in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> who turn judgment to wormwood, and leave off righteousness in the earth,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Seek him]</char> that makes the seven stars (Kimah <char style="pn">(Pleiades)</char> <char style="add">[a cluster]</char>) and Kesil <char style="pn">(Orion)</char> <char style="add">[The Fool]</char>, and turns the shadow of death into the morning, and makes the day dark with night: that calls for the waters of the sea, and pours them out upon the face of the earth: The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> his name:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />That strengthens the spoiled against the strong, so that the spoiled shall come against the fortress.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />They hate him that rebukes in the gate, and they abhor him that speaks uprightly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Forasmuch therefore as your treading <char style="add">[is]</char> upon the poor, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> take from him burdens of wheat: you<char style="ord">2f</char> have built houses of cut stone, but you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not dwell in them; you<char style="ord">2f</char> have planted pleasant vineyards, but you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not drink wine of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />For I know your manifold transgressions and your mighty sins: they afflict the just, they take a bribe, and they turn aside the poor in the gate <char style="add">[from their right]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Therefore the prudent shall keep silence in that time; for it <char style="add">[is]</char> an evil time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Seek good, and not evil, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may live: and so the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, shall be with you, as you<char style="ord">2f</char> have spoken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Hate the evil, and love the good, and establish judgment in the gate: it may be that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> will be gracious unto the remnant of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, says thus; Wailing <char style="add">[shall be]</char> in all streets; and they shall say in all the highways, Alas! alas! and they shall call the farmer to mourning, and such as are skillful of lamentation to wailing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And in all vineyards <char style="add">[shall be]</char> wailing: for I will pass through you<char style="ord">i</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Woe unto you that desire the day of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>! to what end <char style="add">[is]</char> it for you? the day of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> darkness, and not light.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />As if a man did flee from a lion, and a bear met him; or went into the house, and leaned his hand on the wall, and a serpent bit him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Shall]</char> not the day of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> darkness, and not light? even very dark, and no brightness in it?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />I hate, I despise your feast days, and I will not smell in your solemn assemblies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Though you<char style="ord">2f</char> offer me burnt offerings and your meat offerings, I will not accept <char style="add">[them]</char>: neither will I regard the peace offerings of your fat beasts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Take you<char style="ord">i</char> away from me the noise of your<char style="ord">i</char> songs; for I will not hear the melody of your<char style="ord">i</char> viols.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />But let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Have you<char style="ord">2f</char> offered unto me sacrifices and offerings in the wilderness forty years, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">2f</char> have borne the tabernacle of your king and Kiyun <char style="add">[an image or pillar]</char> your images, the star of your god, which you<char style="ord">2f</char> made to yourselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Therefore will I cause you to go into captivity beyond Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, whose name <char style="add">[is]</char> The God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Woe to them <char style="add">[that are]</char> at ease in Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>, and trust in the mountain of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, <char style="add">[which are]</char> named chief of the nations, to whom the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Pass you<char style="ord">2f</char> unto Kalneh <char style="add">[fortress of Anu]</char>, and see; and from there go you<char style="ord">2f</char> to Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> the great: then go down to Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char> of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: <char style="add">[be they]</char> better than these kingdoms? or their border greater than your border?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> that put far away the evil day, and cause the seat of violence to come near;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />That lie upon beds of ivory, and stretch themselves upon their couches, and eat the lambs out of the flock, and the calves out of the midst of the stall;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />That chant to the sound of the viol, <char style="add">[and]</char> invent to themselves instruments of music, like David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />That drink wine in bowls, and anoint themselves with the chief ointments: but they are not grieved for the affliction of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore now shall they go captive with the first that go captive, and the banquet of them that stretched themselves shall be removed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> has sworn by himself, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, I abhor the excellency of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, and hate his palaces: therefore will I deliver up the city with all that is in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, if there remain ten men in one house, that they shall die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And a man’s uncle shall take him up, and he that burns him, to bring out the bones out of the house, and shall say unto him that <char style="add">[is]</char> by the sides of the house, <char style="add">[Is there]</char> yet <char style="add">[any]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>? and he shall say, No. Then shall he say, Hold you<char style="ord">i</char> tongue: for we may not make mention of the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For, behold, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commands, and he will strike the great house with breaches, and the little house with clefts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Shall horses run upon the rock? will <char style="add">[one]</char> plow <char style="add">[there]</char> with oxen? for you<char style="ord">2f</char> have turned judgment into gall <char style="pn">(something bitter or poisonous)</char>, and the fruit of righteousness into hemlock:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> which rejoice in a thing of nothing, which say, Have we not taken to us horns by our own strength?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But, behold, I will raise up against you a nation, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; and they shall afflict you from the entering in of Hamat <char style="add">[fortress]</char> unto the river of the wilderness.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Thus has the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> showed unto me; and, behold, he formed grasshoppers in the beginning of the shooting up of the latter growth; and, lo, <char style="add">[it was]</char> the latter growth after the king’s mowings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it came to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> when they had made an end of eating the grass of the land, then I said, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, forgive, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>: by whom shall Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> arise? for he <char style="add">[is]</char> small.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> repented for this: It shall not be, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Thus has the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> showed unto me: and, behold, the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> called to contend by fire, and it devoured the great deep, and did eat up a part.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then said I, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, cease, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>: by whom shall Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> arise? for he <char style="add">[is]</char> small.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> repented for this: This also shall not be, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Thus he showed me: and, behold, the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> stood upon a wall <char style="add">[made]</char> by a plumbline, with a plumbline in his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto me, ‘Amos <char style="add">[burden]</char>, what see you<char style="ord">i</char>? And I said, A plumbline. Then said the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, Behold, I will set a plumbline in the midst of my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: I will not again pass by them any more:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the high places of Yitz’khak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char> shall be desolate, and the sanctuaries of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall be laid waste; and I will rise against the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> with the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> the priest of Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> sent to Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, ‘Amos <char style="add">[burden]</char> has conspired against you<char style="ord">i</char> in the midst of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: the land is not able to bear all his words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For thus ‘Amos <char style="add">[burden]</char> says, Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> shall die by the sword, and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall surely be led away captive out of their own land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Also Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> said unto ‘Amos <char style="add">[burden]</char>, O you<char style="ord">i</char> seer, go, flee you<char style="ord">i</char> away into the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and there eat bread, and prophesy there:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />But prophesy not again any more at Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>: for it <char style="add">[is]</char> the king’s chapel, and it <char style="add">[is]</char> the king’s court.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then answered ‘Amos <char style="add">[burden]</char>, and said to Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char>, I <char style="add">[was]</char> no prophet, neither <char style="add">[was]</char> I a prophet’s son; but I <char style="add">[was]</char> an herdman, and a gatherer of sycamore fruit:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> took me as I followed the flock, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto me, Go, prophesy unto my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Now therefore hear you<char style="ord">i</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> say, Prophesy not against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and drop not [your<char style="ord">i</char> word] against the house of Yitz’khak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Therefore thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; You<char style="ord">1s</char> wife shall be an prostitute in the city, and your<char style="ord">i</char> sons and your<char style="ord">i</char> daughters shall fall by the sword, and you<char style="ord">i</char> land shall be divided by line; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall die in a polluted land: and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall surely go into captivity forth of his land.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Thus has the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> showed unto me: and behold a basket of summer fruit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he said, ‘Amos <char style="add">[burden]</char>, what see you<char style="ord">i</char>? And I said, A basket of summer fruit. Then said the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto me, The end is come upon my people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; I will not again pass by them any more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the songs of the temple shall be howlings in that day, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>: <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> many dead bodies in every place; they shall cast <char style="add">[them]</char> forth with silence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Hear this, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> that swallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> up the needy, even to make the poor of the land to fail,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Saying, When will the new moon be gone, that we may sell corn? and the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, that we may set forth wheat, making the eifah small, and the shekel great, and falsifying the balances by deceit?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />That we may buy the poor for silver, and the needy for a pair of shoes; <char style="add">[yes]</char>, and sell the refuse of the wheat?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sworn by the excellency of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, Surely I will never forget any of their works.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Shall not the land tremble for this, and everyone mourn that dwells in it? and it shall rise up wholly as a flood; and it shall be cast out and drowned, as <char style="add">[by]</char> the flood of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it shall come to pass in that day, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, that I will cause the sun to go down at noon, and I will darken the earth in the clear day:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And I will turn your feasts into mourning, and all your songs into lamentation; and I will bring up sackcloth upon all waist, and baldness upon every head; and I will make it as the mourning of an only <char style="add">[son]</char>, and the end thereof as a bitter day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Behold, the days come, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, that I will send a famine in the land, not a famine of bread, nor a thirst for water, but of hearing the words of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they shall wander from sea to sea, and from the north even to the east, they shall run to and fro to seek the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and shall not find <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />In that day shall the fair virgins and young men faint for thirst.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />They that swear by the sin of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and say, You<char style="ord">1s</char> god, O Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, lives; and, The manner of Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char> lives; even they shall fall, and never rise up again.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />I saw the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> standing upon the altar: and he said, Strike the lintel <char style="pn">(top of the door frame)</char> of the door, that the posts may shake: and cut them in the head, all of them; and I will slay the last of them with the sword: he that flees of them shall not flee away, and he that escapes of them shall not be delivered.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Though they dig into hell, there shall my hand take them; though they climb up to heaven, there will I bring them down:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And though they hide themselves in the top of Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>, I will search and take them out there; and though they be hid from my sight in the bottom of the sea, there will I command the serpent, and he shall bite them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And though they go into captivity before their enemies, there will I command the sword, and it shall slay them: and I will set my eyes upon them for evil, and not for good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies] [is]</char> he that touches the land, and it shall melt, and all that dwell in it shall mourn: and it shall rise up wholly like a flood; and shall be drowned, as <char style="add">[by]</char> the flood of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[It is]</char> he that builds his stories in the heaven, and has founded his troop in the earth; he that calls for the waters of the sea, and pours them out upon the face of the earth: The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> his name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> not as children of the Ethiopians unto me, O people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. Have not I brought up Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>? and the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> from Kaftor <char style="add">[A Crown]</char>, and the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> from Kir <char style="add">[wall]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Behold, the eyes of the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> upon the sinful kingdom, and I will destroy it from off the face of the earth; saving that I will not utterly destroy the house of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For, lo, I will command, and I will sift the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> among all nations, like as <char style="add">[corn]</char> is sifted in a sieve, yet shall not the least grain fall upon the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />All the sinners of my people shall die by the sword, which say, The evil shall not overtake nor prevent <char style="pn">(come before; go before; anticipate)</char> us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />In that day will I raise up the tabernacle of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> that is fallen, and close up the breaches thereof; and I will raise up his ruins, and I will build it as in the days of old:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />That they may possess the remnant of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and of all the heathen, which are called by my name, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that does this.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Behold, the days come, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that the plowman shall overtake the reaper, and the treader of grapes him that sows seed; and the mountains shall drop sweet wine, and all the hills shall melt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And I will bring again the captivity of my people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and they shall build the waste cities, and inhabit <char style="add">[them]</char>; and they shall plant vineyards, and drink the wine thereof; they shall also make gardens, and eat the fruit of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And I will plant them upon their land, and they shall no more be pulled up out of their land which I have given them, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
</usx>